<title>USA: U.S. corn weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. corn weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. corn major net sales</p>
<p>activity in the week ended Sept 5 reported by exporters for</p>
<p>the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p> Net Sales:	 1996/97		     1997/98</p>
<p>  Unknown	  140,000			    Nil</p>
<p>  Japan	    134,100</p>
<p>  Taiwan	   128,000</p>
<p>  Egypt	     87,000</p>
<p>Sales for the 1996/97 marketing year, which began Sept 1, totaled 644,500 tonnes. A total of 1,001,500 tonnes were outstanding on Aug 31 and were carried over into 1996/97.</p>
<p>Exports of 201,100 tonnes for Aug 30-31 were mainly to Japan, Mexico and Peru. Accumulated exports totaled 55,769,500 tonnes, up 2 percent from 54,742,400 tonnes exported during 1994/95.</p>
<p>Exports for Sept 1-5 totaled 169,100 tonnes, with Egypt, Japan, the Dominican Republic and Mexico the primary destinations.</p>
</text>
